values ('ap_statistics', 1, '1.8', array['1.8', '1.9']::text[], 'diagram', 'Boxplot', 'A boxplot is a graph of the five-number summary, with a box spanning Q1 to Q3, a line at the median, whiskers to the extreme non-outlier values, and outliers marked separately.', '[{"label": "Box", "meaning": "Represents the middle 50% of the data, with ends at Q1 and Q3"}, {"label": "Median line", "meaning": "Line inside the box at the median"}, {"label": "Whiskers", "meaning": "Lines representing 25% of the data each, extending from Q1 to the minimum and from Q3 to the maximum"}, {"label": "Whisker ends when outliers exist", "meaning": "The whiskers extend to the most extreme data values that are not outliers"}, {"label": "Outliers", "meaning": "Usually denoted with an asterisk or other symbol"}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=task0067-reference-pilot-2026-10-09; candidate=ap_statistics-u1-r2-002; ced=1.8.A.2: A boxplot is a graphical representation of the five-number summary (minimum, first quartile, median, third quartile, maximum).')
